  read_tool_result(args: { "result_ref": string; "view"?: "output" | "value"; "offset"?: number /* range 0..* */; "limit"?: number /* range 1..8000 */; "query"?: string })
  {"tool":"read_tool_result","args":{"result_ref":"...","query":"FAILED","limit":4000}}

- done: The application assembles the final JSON. The done arguments object has exactly one property: paragraphs. Do not add summary, report_sections or any other property. Supply natural-language paragraphs in done.paragraphs, one string per paragraph without embedded line breaks, not an inner JSON document. The application joins them with a blank line in /explanation and fills declared receipt-bound fields from committed tool results. Repeat selected values in the explanation only when explicitly required. Explicitly omitted receipt-bound metadata is removed by exact value; other prose is preserved. The required JSON schema describes the application's final output.
  done(args: { "paragraphs": Array<string /* length 1..*; pattern "\\A[^\\r\\n]+\\Z" */> /* items 1..* */ })
